  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ROAP/LA/S1-32QXB-000778 - Enhancing Adaptive Capacity in Lao PDR Provinces, and Building Resilient Housing in Vulnerable Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the project is to build climate resilience in vulnerable, poor communities in six provinces in Lao PDR through improving provincial adaptation capacity, and through building resilience in housing. The project will take a comprehensive approach to increase resilience in shelter and housing by working to improve and localise government adaptation systems as well as strengthening houses and community evacuation centers in selected vulnerable towns. This recognizes that there are many dimensions to building resilience in the housing sector, including policy, planning and regulation; capacity building; strengthening construction practices; and improving early warning and evacuation systems.</narrative>
  </description>
